Here are the Full Specifications for the Smart Grocery Billing System.
🛒 Project Brief
You are building a backend API that takes a list of products, applies specific discounts based on the product category, and generates a final bill.
1️⃣ The Data Structure (Entities)
Class A: Item (Child)
 * Purpose: Represents a single product in the cart.
 * Fields:
   * Long id (PK)
   * String name (e.g., "Apple")
   * String category (e.g., "FRUITS", "ELECTRONICS")
   * double price (e.g., 100.0)
Class B: Bill (Parent)
 * Purpose: Represents the final receipt.
 * Fields:
   * Long id (PK)
   * String customerName
   * double totalAmount (Sum of all prices before discount)
   * double discountedAmount (Total money saved)
   * double finalAmount (Total - Discount)
 * Relationship:
   * One Bill has Many Items.
   * Use @OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL) with a Join Column.
2️⃣ The Data Transfer Objects (DTOs)
Input: BillRequest
 * Fields:
   * String customerName
   * List<Item> items (The list of products the user wants to buy)
Output: BillResponse
 * Fields:
   * Long billId
   * String customerName
   * double totalAmount
   * double discountedAmount
   * double finalAmount
3️⃣ The Logic Core (Service Layer) 🧠
This is the most important part. Inside your createBill method, you must:
 * Initialize Variables:
   * double total = 0;
   * double discount = 0;
 * The Loop: Iterate through every Item in the list.
 * The Math (Inside Loop):
   * Add the item's price to total.
   * Check Category:
     * If category is "FRUITS" -> Calculate 10% of price and add to discount.
     * If category is "ELECTRONICS" -> Calculate 5% of price and add to discount.
     * Else -> No discount.
 * Final Calculation (Outside Loop):
   * finalAmount = total - discount
 * Save & Return:
   * Save the Bill (which automatically saves Items).
   * Return the BillResponse.
4️⃣ The API Endpoint (Controller)
 * Method: POST
 * URL: /billing/create
 * Body: Expects BillRequest.
